tsani@mail.jerrington.me> wrote:

>  On 07/15/2015 09:51 AM, la durka wrote:
>
>  and it means it's no longer possible to quickly scan a text for {.i} to
> separate the sentences -- you need to parse the entire text to find the
> sentence boundaries.
>
> We can't really just scan the text for {.i} as it may be quoted,
> specifically by {lu...li'u}.
>

Or it could be grabbed by a magic word: ".i bu" ".i zei da", etc. Because
of magic words, there's not much you can do with a Lojban text by just
scanning for words, you always need to parse first in order to know whether
the words are fulfilling their usual functions or not.

